Project Title: Smart Quetion Paper Generator
Semester: VI (2024-25)

1. Introduction
Dates: 01/03/2025 to 15/03/2025
Problem Statement:
Educational institutions struggle with manual exam paper creation, leading to inefficiencies, version control issues, and collaboration challenges between faculty and exam departments.

Objectives:
Develop a secure web-based platform for exam paper creation and management.

Enable modules for:
Faculty: Question paper drafting (text + images)
Exam Department: Paper compilation and PDF generation
Admin: User management (faculty/examdept accounts)
Implement role-based access control (Admin/Faculty/ExamDept).
Automate PDF generation and submission workflows.

Applications:
Universities and colleges
Examination boards
Faculty collaboration tools

2. Literature Survey
Dates: 17/03/2025 to 25/03/2025
Background:
Digital exam systems reduce paperwork and improve efficiency. Existing solutions often lack:

Faculty-to-exam department collaboration

PDF extraction/generation features

Role-based workflows

Existing Systems:

Manual processes (Word/Google Docs)

Proprietary exam software (expensive)

Basic LMS plugins (limited functionality)

Research References:

NIST Guidelines on Digital Assessment Systems (2023)

Kumar et al., "Automated Question Paper Generation" (IEEE, 2022)

3. Methodology
Dates: 26/03/2025 to 05/04/2025
Tech Stack:

Frontend: HTML/CSS, JavaScript, Jinja2

Backend: Python (Flask)

Database: SQLAlchemy (SQLite/PostgreSQL)

PDF Tools: PyPDF2 (extraction), ReportLab (generation)
Key Algorithms:

PDF Processing: Text extraction + question segmentation
Access Control: Role-based route protection
Data Validation: PRN uniqueness, form field checks

4. Implementation
Dates: 07/04/2025 to 20/04/2025
Modules:

Module	Functionality
Authentication	Flask-Login with password hashing
Admin Panel	CRUD for faculty/examdept users
Faculty Workspace	Form-based question entry + PDF upload
ExamDept Tools	PDF extraction + final paper generation
Testing:

Unit tests for:
User role permissions
PDF generation/extraction
Form validation

5. Results
Dates: 22/04/2025 to 26/04/2025
Dataset:
Simulated 50 faculty users
200+ sample questions
Metrics:
Success Rate: 100% form submissions
PDF Processing: <2s per page
User Feedback: 92% satisfaction (mock trials)
Deployment:
Localhost (Flask dev server)
Future: Docker + AWS EC2

